
=== 2026-09-02T17:32Z :: /home/ubuntu/Liars_Are_Information/.venv/bin/python /home/ubuntu/Liars_Are_Information/scripts/phase_b_correlation.py --help ===
usage: phase_b_correlation.py [-h] [--cache CACHE] [--cache-t07 CACHE_T07]
                              [--out OUT] [--figure FIGURE]
                              [--resamples RESAMPLES] [--seed SEED]
                              [--config CONFIG]

Phase B: pairwise error correlation and blind-estimator validation. **Cache-
only.** This script never loads a model. It reads the Phase A parquet caches
read-only and writes analysis artefacts; if it ever needs new inference, that
is a bug to report rather than an action to take. It answers the headline
question -- whether a homogeneous swarm is epistemically one agent -- and
validates the attenuation-law estimator that lets an agent measure pair
quality from broadcasts alone, with no labels.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --cache CACHE
  --cache-t07 CACHE_T07
  --out OUT
  --figure FIGURE
  --resamples RESAMPLES
  --seed SEED
  --config CONFIG

